# CalcWise Content Standards

## Absolute Rules

1. **NO emoji** — use SVG icons from `src/components/Icons.tsx`
2. **NO generic filler** — every paragraph must contain specific numbers, examples, or actionable advice
3. **English only** — all content targets US/UK audience
4. **Domain** — site URL is `https://www.calcwise.tools`
5. **Privacy** — all calculations client-side, never collect user financial data
6. **No HTML entities in JSX text** — in this toolchain a multi-line JSX text node that contains `&apos;`, `&quot;`, `&amp;` etc. loses the space after a preceding inline element (renders "Label:text"). Write literal characters (`'`, `"`, `&`, `’`, `→`, `÷`) in JSX text; use `{"<"}` for a literal less-than sign. Also put `{" "}` after an inline element that ends a line when text continues on the next line. After editing, check built HTML: `rg "</(strong|a|em|b)>[A-Za-z0-9]" .next/server/app` should return nothing.

## Content Quality Requirements

### For Calculator Articles (800+ words)
- Include the mathematical formula with variable explanations
- At least 1 concrete example with real dollar amounts
- At least 1 comparison (15yr vs 30yr, different rates, etc.)
- 3-5 FAQ questions at the end
- Internal links to 2-3 related calculators
- At least 1 infographic image (use kie-image skill, 3:2 ratio, 2K resolution)

### For Guide Articles (1500+ words)
- Start with a specific problem/question
- Include a TL;DR / quick answer near the top
- At least 1 detailed case study with a named persona
- At least 1 data comparison table
- Step-by-step actionable instructions
- Calculator CTA linking to relevant tool
- FAQ section with JSON-LD schema
- At least 1 infographic image

### For Variant Pages (Programmatic SEO)
- Unique intro text explaining the specific scenario
- 3-5 scenario-specific tips/considerations with concrete dollar amounts
- Pre-filled calculator with sensible defaults
- Internal links to related variants
- 3-4 scenario-specific FAQ entries (`faq` field) with FaqJsonLd
- 4-6 pre-calculated key results (`keyResults` field) shown in a summary table
- A `comparisonNote` (2-3 sentences) explaining how this scenario compares to adjacent variants
- Data structure: all variant data uses `CalculatorVariant` from `src/lib/variants/types.ts`

### Information Gain Gate for Variant Pages
Before creating a new variant, it MUST pass these checks:
1. **Unique question test** — does this variant answer a question that no other page on the site answers?
2. **Strategy differentiation** — does the advice genuinely differ from other variants of the same calculator? (Changing dollar amounts alone is NOT enough.)
3. **Minimum 500 unique words** — intro + tips + FAQ answers + comparisonNote must total at least 500 words of unique text
4. **No pure-number variants** — avoid creating variants that only differ by a dollar amount or percentage (e.g., "$5K balance" vs "$10K balance" for the same strategy). Instead, consolidate number-based breakdowns into a guide article with anchored sections.
5. **Maximum 5-7 variants per calculator** — quality over quantity

## Image Generation (kie-image) & Post-Processing

Always use for infographics in articles. All images MUST be webp format, max 1200px wide.

### Generation + Conversion Pipeline

```bash
# 1. Generate image
node ~/.cursor/skills/kie-image/generate.mjs "[prompt]" "3:2" --resolution 2K

# 2. Download as temp PNG
curl -o /tmp/temp-image.png "[result_url]"

# 3. Resize to 1200px wide and convert to webp (quality 80)
sips --resampleWidth 1200 /tmp/temp-image.png --out /tmp/temp-resized.png
cwebp -q 80 /tmp/temp-resized.png -o public/images/[name].webp

# 4. Clean up temp files
rm /tmp/temp-image.png /tmp/temp-resized.png
```

For guides, save to `public/images/guides/[slug].webp`.
For calculator articles, save to `public/images/[slug]-infographic.webp`.

Good prompt patterns:
- "Clean minimal infographic on white background showing [concept]. [specific data/labels]. Blue and green color scheme. Professional financial style, no decorative elements, data-focused."
- "Simple comparison chart on white background. Left: [option A]. Right: [option B]. [specific numbers]. Clean professional design."
- "Timeline infographic showing [financial journey]. [milestones with dollar amounts]. Horizontal layout. Blue color scheme. Minimal professional style."

Use with `next/image` (dimensions will be 1200x800 for 3:2 ratio, 1200x675 for 16:9):
```tsx
<Image src="/images/[name].webp" alt="[descriptive]" width={1200} height={800} className="rounded-lg border border-ink-200" />
```

## SEO Requirements

- Every page has unique `title` (50-60 chars) and `description` (120-155 chars)
- Breadcrumb navigation on all pages except home
- Internal links: each page should link to 2-4 other pages on the site
- Heading hierarchy: one H1, logical H2/H3 structure
- Image alt text: descriptive, includes relevant keyword naturally
- URL structure: `/calculators/[slug]`, `/guides/[slug]`, `/calculators/[slug]/[variant]`

## Tech Stack Reference

- Framework: Next.js 16 (App Router, SSG)
- Styling: Tailwind CSS 4 with custom theme in globals.css
- Icons: Custom SVG components in `src/components/Icons.tsx`
- Data: TypeScript files in `src/lib/`
- Deployment: Vercel (auto-deploy on push to main)
- Domain: www.calcwise.tools (calcwise.tools 301 → www)
